<header><p class="st-kicker">other · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Angevin Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">1154 CE – 1214 CE · capital Chinon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The vast assemblage of lands ruled by Henry II and his sons, from the Scottish border to the Pyrenees, which collapsed in the wars with Philip II.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II</a> inherited <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-anjou">Anjou</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-maine">Maine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/touraine">Touraine</a> from his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geoffrey-plantagenet-count-of-anjou">Geoffrey Plantagenet</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Normandy</a> through his mother Matilda, gained <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Aquitaine</a> by marrying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine">Eleanor of Aquitaine</a> in 1152, and became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1154. He also asserted lordship over Ireland from 1171 and over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-brittany">Brittany</a> through his son Geoffrey.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>There was no single government: each land kept its own customs, though Henry built strong royal justice in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and moved constantly between his territories. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinon">Chinon</a> was a favourite residence and treasury. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry's</a> sons rebelled repeatedly, backed by the French kings. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> spent most of his reign on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, building <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chateau-gaillard">Château Gaillard</a> to guard <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Normandy</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> lost <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Normandy</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-anjou">Anjou</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-maine">Maine</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip II</a> in 1202–1204, and his allies' defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bouvines">Bouvines</a> in 1214 ended hopes of recovery. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>, and the term Angevin Empire was coined by modern historians.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/angevin-empire.jpg" alt="Angevin Empire" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Britannicus the Scot · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Angevin_Empire.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1154 CE – 1214 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chinon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Henry II of England, Richard I of England, John of England</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a>, <a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Plantagenet lands</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1184&amp;focus=angevin-empire" aria-label="Angevin Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4686 522 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Angevin Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5006 778L5025 711M5006 778L4970 663M5006 778L5054 